	quest.33650D70A29FC3E3.quest_desc: [
		"All of the shaders have visual bugs, such as Photon not displaying Honey Glue, try disabling or using a different one temporarily if you have problems"
		""
		"Due to the mod I'm using for space stuff having issues with shaders you &cMUST!&r use Complementary while in orbit or on the moon, the other planets still kinda make sense with the other shaders so it's up to you if you want to bother switching them depending on where you are or just leave Complementary on all the time."
		""
		"The Modpack comes with 2 shaders installed, but my favorite is Eclipse, which is only on GitHub, If you'd like to try it out you can download it below but you &cMUST!&r delete \"gbuffers_terrain.gsh\", \"gbuffers_terrain.tcs\" and \"gbuffers_terrain.tes\" files for all world folders in the shader .zip for it to work."
		""
		"[ \"\", { \"text\": \"https://github.com/Merlin1809/Eclipse-Shader\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"open_url\", \"value\": \"https://github.com/Merlin1809/Eclipse-Shader\" } } ]"
		""
		"Eclipse and Photon both have upscaling turned on for better frame rate but if it bothers you or you are already getting good enough performance you can disable them in the shader settings."
		""
		"Read the quest \"Getting More FPS\" in the help chapter if Photon is still too heavy for your PC."
	]
