	quest.377D6D61ACEA0D85.title: "Andesite Alloy"
	quest.37F3F3C43FE56625.quest_desc: [
		"While I've highly customized most of the mod settings, you might not like some of them, here is a list of things that might be bothering you and how to change them if want. You can change the configs by pausing the game and clicking on \"Mods\" the seachring for the name of the mod then click \"Config\" in the bottom left."
		""
		"New font: Modern UI, you can change the font in the config or remove the mod. The inventory item count font is from Reliable Recount, you can remove it."
		""
		"Dynamic Crosshair: Dynamic Crosshair, the config is pretty customizable but you can also just remove it."
		""
		"Hand Movement Animations: Fresh Animations Resorcepack, you can disable it."
		""
		"Dark UI: Dark Mode Everywhere, use the button on the main menu to change, no need to remove it"
		""
		"Quest completion popup: FancyToasts, you can remove the mod."
		""
		"Camera effects: CameraOverhaul, you can remove the mod."
		""
		"Star on newly picked up items: Item Highlighter, you can remove the mod."
		""
		"Turn on minimap: Open map (M) > Open settings in top left > Minimap Settings > Minimap ON"
		""
		"EMI Groups: Reliable EMI > Groups, uncheck Enable."
		""
		"The world is too big: Tectonic config settings."
		""
		"Weight of blocks in Jade: Jade Sable Compat, you can remove the mod."
		""
		"Grass on grass blocks: Resource Packs > Grassy_Grass."
		""
		"Trees falling: Panda's Falling Trees, you can sneak break the trees normally, or remove the mod."
		""
		"Longer days and nights: BetterDays > Time Settings, or remove the mod."
		""
		"Biome name popup: Traveler's Titles, you can remove the mod."
		""
		"Terralith Skylands: Disabled by it's config. you can reenable them if you want."
		""
		"Changing of Seasons: Serene Seasons, you can remove the mod. (If you remove it while there is snow created from the mod on the ground, it will NOT MELT, wait until it's gone)"
	]
	quest.37F3F3C43FE56625.title: "Customizing the modpack"
